  "description": "Multi-layer recovery system covering physical, emotional, social, relational, institutional, and narrative recovery. Integrates with state transitions, scene engine, and event sourcing.",
  "design_principles": {
    "principle_1": "Recovery is a state transition, not a scene end.",
    "principle_2": "Every character has recovery needs that vary by character, context, and intensity of the preceding event.",
    "principle_3": "Recovery is not linear. A character may need multiple recovery phases.",
    "principle_4": "Neglecting recovery produces cascading penalties.",
    "principle_5": "Recovery can be self-directed, partner-directed, or institution-directed.",
    "principle_6": "Recovery is tracked per character and per relationship."
  },

